# .private-terms — your own wordlist of things that must never appear in a committed file.
#
# Copy this file to `.private-terms` (gitignored — never committed, so the wordlist itself never
# leaks the very things it's protecting) and fill in your own: your real name/surname, real
# employer names, unreleased product codenames, anything else that would be a problem if it
# showed up in engine code, a commit message, or a doc file.
#
# One term per line, plain substring match (case-sensitive). Blank lines and lines starting with
# # are ignored. scripts/audit_public.py reads this automatically if it exists at the repo root.
#
# Example entries (fake, just showing the shape):
# Jane Doe
# Acme Robotics Inc
# Project Nightingale
